### Aged Care Reporting Requirements in South Australia

#### **1. Aged Care Quality and Safety Commission**
- **Serious Incident Response Scheme (SIRS)**: Providers must report serious incidents, including abuse, neglect, and unexplained absences, within specific timeframes. Priority 1 incidents must be reported within 24 hours [1](https://www.agedcarequality.gov.au/workers/reporting-incidents).
- **Incident Management System**: Providers must have an effective incident management system to continuously improve how they manage and prevent incidents [1](https://www.agedcarequality.gov.au/workers/reporting-incidents).

#### **2. Australian Government Department of Health and Aged Care**
- **Financial and Operational Reporting**: Providers must submit regular financial and operational reports, including the Aged Care Financial Report (ACFR) and Quarterly Financial Report (QFR) [2](https://www.health.gov.au/topics/aged-care/providing-aged-care-services/reporting).
- **Quality Indicators**: Providers must report on quality indicators as part of the National Aged Care Mandatory Quality Indicator Program [2](https://www.health.gov.au/topics/aged-care/providing-aged-care-services/reporting).

#### **3. Aged Care Act 1997 (Cth)**
- **Mandatory Reporting**: Providers must report incidents of elder abuse, including physical, sexual, and financial abuse, as well as neglect [3](https://agedcaredecisions.com.au/what-is-mandatory-reporting-in-aged-care/).
- **Compliance and Sanctions**: Providers must comply with the Aged Care Act and may face sanctions for non-compliance [3](https://agedcaredecisions.com.au/what-is-mandatory-reporting-in-aged-care/).

#### **4. Public Health Act 2011 (SA)**
- **Notifiable Disease Reporting**: Providers must report any notifiable diseases to public health authorities as required by law [3](https://agedcaredecisions.com.au/what-is-mandatory-reporting-in-aged-care/).

These requirements ensure comprehensive documentation, transparency, and accountability within the aged care system, aiming to improve the safety and quality of care provided to older Australians.

